  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1253 PM CDT Sun Sep 6 2026\n\nThe strong upper ridge will break down over the northern part of\nthe country, but continue to control the weather over the southern\nstates. Southeasterly low level flow will keep hot, moist air over\nSouth-Central Texas. There may be some seabreeze convection each\nday Tuesday through Thursday over the Coastal Plains, but chances\nare low. Most of the area will be hot and dry. Temperatures will\nbe steady and above normal through the week. The NBM is showing\nhigher humidity into the week, but it has tended to run moist in\nthe medium term. The forecast higher dewpoints have not developed.\nHowever, if the higher dewpoints verify we will reach Heat\nAdvisory criteria over the Coastal Plains and I-35 Corridor by\nmid-week.",
